###  https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120093
:MILD_120093 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                rdfs:subClassOf obo:OMRSE_00000012 ;
                                                                obo:IAO_0000115 "A healthcare provider role that inheres in a person in virtue of that person being licensed to practice medicine."@en ;
                                                                rdfs:comment "Relocated from WONT_0000090 when the MILD/WONT import direction was reversed: a physician role is not wound-specific, is not used by any WONT class, and its only consumer is the MILD treatment-plan axiom. Reuse an OMRSE physician-role class here if an OMRSE module is later added."@en ;
                                                                rdfs:label "Physician role"@en .


###  https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120098
:MILD_120098 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                rdfs:subClassOf obo:IAO_0000033 ;
                                                                obo:IAO_0000115 "A directive information entity that has as part a threshold value and a comparison operator and that is about a quality, such that the quality's meeting the threshold is what the specification prescribes as decisive."@en ;
                                                                obo:IAO_0000116 "Generalises the disease threshold specification (MILD_120029), which is the special case about a phenotypic abnormality. Other specifications with the same shape - a wound healing criterion, an outcome criterion in a trial protocol - are about qualities that are not abnormalities, so they need a parent that does not say 'disease'. Lives in MILD because WONT and any other domain ontology need it and MILD never imports them."@en ;
                                                                rdfs:label "threshold specification"@en .


